INT. COMMUNITY POOL LOCKER ROOM - EARLY MORNING

Wet tile. Green-tinted mirrors. A bank of dented lockers. A radio plays a pop song through a haze of chlorine.

LOLA FERREIRA-OKORO (17, towel on her shoulder, hair in a wet braid) sits on a bench, tying a shoe. TARIQ MONTGOMERY-HASSAN (17, swim team jacket) leans against the lockers, scrolling his phone. And their friend PRIYA DESAI-LUND (17, goggles pushed up on her head) stands at a mirror, practicing a speech.

PRIYA
(to the mirror)
Ahem. Fellow students. I stand before you today...

TARIQ
You look like a politician.

PRIYA
That's the idea.

LOLA
You're running for class president?

PRIYA
Treasurer.

TARIQ
Treasurer? Who runs for treasurer?

PRIYA
Someone who wants the budget.

LOLA
She wants the prom budget.

TARIQ
^She wants the prom budget.

PRIYA
I want a prom that doesn't have a cardboard castle.

LOLA
I loved the castle.

PRIYA
It fell on Mr. Dunphy.

TARIQ
It was a great fall.

Priya turns from the mirror. Crosses her arms.

PRIYA
Will you two vote for me or not?

LOLA
Obviously.

TARIQ
(muttering)
Define "vote."

PRIYA
Tariq.

TARIQ
Fine. Yes. I'll vote for you.

PRIYA
Say it like you mean it.

TARIQ
I'll vote for you, Priya Desai-Lund, future Treasurer of the senior class.

LOLA
Thank you, Tariq.

TARIQ
(to the room)
Does anyone else need me to affirm anything?

LOLA
Not at the moment.

Priya claps once, delighted. The radio changes songs. A locker door bangs somewhere and all three flinch.

PRIYA
Who's there?

No answer. Tariq edges to the end of the row, peers around the corner.

TARIQ
Nobody. Just the wind.

LOLA
There's no wind in a locker room.

TARIQ
Then it's a ghost.

PRIYA
It's the janitor.

LOLA
It's the castle.

They laugh, shoving each other toward the exit. The radio hums. The door swings shut.
